TurboQuant fused-MMA flash-attention fix for head_dim 256 models (e.g. qwen35moe / Tiel-Coder)

Applies to: https://github.com/thecodacus/llama.cpp  branch `perf`, commit 27c54b4
Source:     https://github.com/thecodacus/llama.cpp/pull/12 by wilky2005 (unmerged upstream at time of writing)

Fixes two bugs in the turbo2/3/4 KV-cache fused MMA decode path:
  1. fattn-mma-turbo.cuh: launch_fattn() was called without the `use_sparse` argument, shifting
     `warp_size_host` into that slot -> n_kv_max == 0 -> GGML_ASSERT(n_kv_max > 0) at warmup.
  2. fattn-mma-f16.cuh: turbo tile loaders ignored the SMEM XOR-swizzle that head_dim 256
     enables, silently scrambling attention (wrong answers) even when it did not crash.

Apply with:  git -C <llama.cpp-perf checkout> apply turboquant-pr12-fix.patch

